Windows distributables: NSIS installer + portable exe (CI-built)

Extends the packaging with Windows targets, built natively in CI:

- win targets in electron-builder.yml: NSIS (assisted installer,
  changeable install directory) + a single-file portable exe, named
  Grungus-Setup-<v>.exe and Grungus-<v>-portable.exe.
- scripts/make-icon.py now also emits build/icon.ico — a valid
  multi-size ICO (16/24/32/48/64/128/256, PNG-embedded entries,
  little-endian ICONDIR; verified entry-by-entry). The earlier draft
  on disk was broken twice over: it recursed via subprocess with no
  __main__ guard (infinite child spawning) and packed the ICO
  big-endian; both fixed by the single-process scale-parameterized
  rewrite.
- New CI job "Package Windows distributables" on windows-latest:
  npm ci, esbuild bundle, electron-builder --win, uploading the
  installers as the grungus-windows artifact.

Windows builds are CI-ONLY by design: cross-building win targets on
Linux needs wine for rcedit (embedding the icon/version into the
exe), and this system deliberately stays wine-free — verified before
this change that no wine exists anywhere (no dpkg package, no
binaries in system paths, no prefixes/caches in user space). The
npm run dist:win script exists for native Windows checkouts.

Suite 86/86, tsc clean; the Windows artifacts are verified by the CI
run itself (upload with if-no-files-found: error guarantees the exes
exist).
